<title>FRANCE: Kohl says does not want changes to stability pact.</title>
<headline>Kohl says does not want changes to stability pact.</headline>
<dateline>POITIERS, France 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said on Friday that he did not wish to see any changes made to the stability pact, a pact designed to secure fiscal austerity after the introduction of the euro.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference after regular French-German consultations, Kohl said &quot;What we certainly do not want is any change to the stability pact as it has already been agreed.&quot;</p>
<p>Kohl also said it was too early to comment on the new French government's social demands, saying he had not yet studied them in detail.</p>
<p>He affirmed however that Germany did not back any measures which would require fund transfers to Brussels.</p>
</text>
